@page "/virtualized"

<PageTitle>Virtualize + KeepRegistered</PageTitle>
<h1>Virtualize + KeepRegistered</h1>
<p>200 rows in a virtualized container. KeepRegistered keeps scrolled-away rows registered, and a DisclosureOverride reveals the whole collection — so the summary reports every row's errors from the first submit, and the focus fallback scrolls far rows into view on click.</p>

<TeachingPanel CodeFiles="@(new[] { "Virtualized.razor", "Virtualized.razor.cs", "GadgetOrder.cs" })">
    <Rules>
        <ul>
            <li>Every row's <strong>Serial</strong> is required. A committed change to the field discloses it, no submit needed. Every 7th row starts empty — 28 errors across 200 rows.</li>
            <li>Disclosure is render-registration: a row can show issues once it has rendered. <code>KeepRegistered</code> keeps scrolled-past rows disclosed after they leave the window.</li>
            <li>This page also sets a <code>DisclosureOverride</code> for the collection, so the summary lists every row's errors from the first submit — even rows Virtualize has never rendered. Validation always runs against the full in-memory model; only <em>visibility</em> is render-gated, so the override costs nothing.</li>
            <li>Clicking a never-rendered row's entry uses the summary's <code>FocusFallback</code>: scroll the panel, let the row render, retry the focus. A blocked submit's own auto-focus uses the form's matching <code>FocusFallback</code> the same way, whenever the first error it lands on is itself off-screen.</li>
        </ul>
    </Rules>
    <TryIt>
        <ol>
            <li>Submit immediately — the summary lists all 28 missing serials, no scrolling required.</li>
            <li>Click an entry near the top — it focuses directly.</li>
            <li>Click one of the LAST entries — the panel scrolls, the row renders, and focus lands. That is the fallback at work.</li>
            <li>Fix one of the missing serials and tab out of the box — its entry leaves the summary there and then, with no submit: committing the change engages that row, and the live channel answers for it. The other 27 stay listed.</li>
            <li>Scroll far away from that row and submit again — its entry stays gone even with nothing on screen rendering it, and all 27 of the others are still listed.</li>
        </ol>
    </TryIt>
</TeachingPanel>

<FormidableForm Model="_order" Options="_options" OnValidSubmit="HandleValid" FocusFallback="ScrollToRowAsync">
    <div class="summary-slot">
        <FormidableSummary FocusFallback="ScrollToRowAsync" />
    </div>

    <div class="scroll-panel">
        <Virtualize Items="_order.Gadgets" ItemSize="RowHeight" Context="gadget">
            <div class="field" @key="gadget">
                <label>Serial
                    <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="gadget.Serial" KeepRegistered="true" />
                </label>
                <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => gadget.Serial" />
            </div>
        </Virtualize>
    </div>

    <div class="actions"><button type="submit">Submit</button></div>
</FormidableForm>

<p role="status">@_status</p>
